# NetNebula crawler settings.
#
# Copy to `.env` next to this file and edit. `.env` is git-ignored; this
# template is not, so it must never hold a real value.
#
#   cp scrapper/.env.example scrapper/.env
#
# Every line below is optional: the defaults shown are the ones compiled into
# crawler.py, and an exported shell variable always wins over the file.

# -- credentials ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the Firebase service account key. Needed only against the real
# database; the emulator authenticates nobody. Point one of these at a file
# kept outside the repository.
#GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/serviceAccountKey.json
#NN_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=/absolute/path/to/serviceAccountKey.json

# -- local emulator ------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this and the crawler writes to the local emulator instead: no quota, a
# throwaway database. Must match firebase.json > emulators > firestore.
#FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8088
#GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=netnebula-local

# -- politeness ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Sent on every request, and the name robots.txt rules are matched against.
# Keep a reachable contact URL in it.
#NN_USER_AGENT=NetNebulaBot/1.0 (+https://github.com/SPTApyo/NetNebula)

# Honour robots.txt. Turn it off only for a host you own.
#NN_OBEY_ROBOTS=1

# Simultaneous connections to a single host. Also a concurrency ceiling: real
# throughput is min(NN_WORKERS, NN_PER_HOST x distinct hosts in flight).
#NN_PER_HOST=8

# -- quota guards --------------------------------------------------------------
# The Firebase Spark plan allows 20000 writes and 50000 reads per day. A run
# stops on its own before the budget runs out and resumes on the next launch.
#NN_WRITE_BUDGET=18000
#NN_MAX_PAGES=500000

# Ceiling on the frontier: every URL discovered, taken or not. Separate from
# NN_MAX_PAGES, because one page discovers dozens of links. It bounds the cost
# of resuming: the frontier is read in full at startup.
#NN_MAX_FRONTIER=30000

# -- crawl shape ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Hops allowed outside the whitelist. 1: the direct neighbour of a known
# domain, not the neighbour of that neighbour.
#NN_MAX_OUTSIDE=1

# Content links kept per page. All of them turns the graph into a clump.
#NN_MAX_LINKS_PER_PAGE=60

# Pages taken from one domain before it yields the turn.
#NN_DOMAIN_BLOCK=50

# -- throughput ----------------------------------------------------------------
#NN_WORKERS=16
#NN_FETCH_TIMEOUT=15
#NN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
